Research Project Scope

Project Title

Scheduling Packets for a Rural Environment with Constraints

Research Question

How do FIFO, Priority Queuing (PQ), and Weighted Fair Queuing (WFQ) compare in terms of throughput, packet delay, packet loss, and flow fairness under simulated bandwidth-constrained network conditions?

Research Aim

To evaluate and compare the performance of FIFO, PQ, and WFQ scheduling algorithms in a simulated bandwidth-constrained network environment using MAWI traffic traces.

Research Objectives

1. Examine the operating principles of FIFO, PQ and WFQ.
2. Obtain and prepare suitable MAWI network traffic traces.
3. Implement and test the three scheduling algorithms under controlled network conditions.
4. Measure throughput, packet delay, packet loss and flow fairness.
5. Compare results and identify the strengths and limitations of each algorithm.

Dataset

MAWI Working Group Traffic Archive:
https://mawi.wide.ad.jp/mawi/

Research Plan

The group will use a quantitative experimental approach to compare the three scheduling algorithms under identical simulated network conditions. Results will be analysed using comparative tables and graphs.